$ help
Available commands:
change-remote - Changes the remote address used in the tunnel for the provided vpn addr
close-tunnel - Closes a tunnel for the provided vpn addr
create-tunnel - Creates a tunnel for the provided vpn address
device-info - Prints information about the network device.
help - prints available commands or help <command> for specific usage info
identity - Prints the certificate identity of this node, or of the host owning the provided vpn addr
list-hostmap - List all known previously connected hosts
list-lighthouse-addrmap - List all lighthouse map entries
list-pending-hostmap - List all handshaking hosts
log-format - Gets or sets the current log format
log-level - Gets or sets the current log level
mutex-profile-fraction - Gets or sets runtime.SetMutexProfileFraction
print-cert - Prints the current certificate being used or the certificate for the provided vpn addr
print-relays - Prints json details about all relay info
print-tunnel - Prints json details about a tunnel for the provided vpn addr
query-lighthouse - Query the lighthouses for the provided vpn address
reload - Reloads configuration from disk, same as sending HUP to the process
save-heap-profile - Saves a heap profile to the provided path, ex: `heap-profile.pb.gz`
save-mutex-profile - Saves a mutex profile to the provided path, ex: `mutex-profile.pb.gz`
start-cpu-profile - Starts a cpu profile and write output to the provided file, ex: `cpu-profile.pb.gz`
stop-cpu-profile - Stops a cpu profile and writes output to the previously provided file
version - Prints the currently running version of nebula


$ help -json
[{"name":"change-remote","short":"Changes the remote address used in the tunnel for the provided vpn addr","flags":[{"name":"address","usage":"The new remote address, ip:port"},{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"close-tunnel","short":"Closes a tunnel for the provided vpn addr","flags":[{"name":"local-only","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"Disables notifying the remote that the tunnel is shutting down"},{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"create-tunnel","short":"Creates a tunnel for the provided vpn address","help":"The lighthouses will be queried for real addresses but you can provide one as well.","flags":[{"name":"address","usage":"Optionally provide a real remote address, ip:port "},{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"device-info","short":"Prints information about the network device.","flags":[{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"help","short":"prints available commands or help \u003ccommand\u003e for specific usage info","flags":[{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"identity","short":"Prints the certificate identity of this node, or of the host owning the provided vpn addr","help":"Identity is what the certificate says: name, vpn addrs, networks, groups, fingerprint, issuer and validity. The address may carry a port, so a connection's remote address can be passed through as is.","flags":[{"name":"address","usage":"The vpn addr to look up, optionally with a port; this node when omitted"},{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"list-hostmap","short":"List all known previously connected hosts","flags":[{"name":"by-index","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"gets all hosts in the hostmap from the index table"},{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"list-lighthouse-addrmap","short":"List all lighthouse map entries","flags":[{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"list-pending-hostmap","short":"List all handshaking hosts","flags":[{"name":"by-index","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"gets all hosts in the hostmap from the index table"},{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"log-format","short":"Gets or sets the current log format","flags":[{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"log-level","short":"Gets or sets the current log level","flags":[{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"mutex-profile-fraction","short":"Gets or sets runtime.SetMutexProfileFraction","flags":[{"name":"json","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"outputs as json"},{"name":"pretty","bool":true,"default":"false","usage":"pretty prints json, assumes -json"}]},{"name":"